Cell[TextData[{
 "To compile an ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["n", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Source Sans Pro",ExpressionUUID->
  "e1a9f15c-7daa-42be-900a-160efb8be91a"],
 "-ary cyclic tag system to a cyclic tag system, each symbol ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["s", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Source Sans Pro",ExpressionUUID->
  "e4a8021b-0ef8-4417-a59d-b26c82f28f4e"],
 " becomes a block of ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["n", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Source Sans Pro",ExpressionUUID->
  "50fbfc15-e946-4e2e-8de4-e6c44f5cad06"],
 " cells that are all 0 except for a 1 at position ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["s", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Source Sans Pro",ExpressionUUID->
  "487a381f-47f5-4809-b052-7c91544d67f5"],
 "+1, and each rule part becomes ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["n", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Source Sans Pro",ExpressionUUID->
  "a97b0f70-2c4d-4ed3-be7a-e34596a74cd3"],
 " appendants, one for each symbol. Only the 1 in a block makes the cyclic \
tag system append anything, and it does so exactly when the appendant for the \
block's symbol is current. So ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["n", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Source Sans Pro",ExpressionUUID->
  "028d2d56-188c-4c32-80e8-a9f86c6fbbde"],
 " cyclic tag steps emulate one ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["n", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Source Sans Pro",ExpressionUUID->
  "9230f3ad-3cea-4e57-87ba-8e2909e6dbb9"],
 "-ary step."
}], "TechNoteText",
 CellID->619584675,ExpressionUUID->"06bde652-ea67-4263-929b-3976b437af7c"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "A symbol that no rule part ever appends for is a symbol the compiled system \
can never read, so its column is left out of the encoding. That is what ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"\"\<Optimization\>\"", " ", "->", 
   " ", "\"\<DeletedSymbolsHighest\>\""}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Source Sans Pro",ExpressionUUID->
  "594a2a8b-5c06-4b3d-afba-7d6e40748336"],
 ", the default, does: it makes every block narrower and every ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["n", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Source Sans Pro",ExpressionUUID->
  "fc56edea-01d5-4323-9725-63202a1f06d5"],
 "-ary step cheaper, which is where most of the saving in compiling oblivious \
ring machines comes from. The price is that the decoded evolution is the ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["n", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Source Sans Pro",ExpressionUUID->
  "12a75cb8-625d-4194-9bf4-f9517234e8e1"],
 "-ary one with its symbols renumbered: the symbols that survive are renamed \
to their positions among the survivors, and the ones left out all decode to \
one label that no surviving symbol uses. When there is nothing to leave out, \
the decoded evolution is identical to the ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["n", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Source Sans Pro",ExpressionUUID->
  "49f63bfb-966c-4a98-b4ed-3f5f0b0d8f56"],
 "-ary one."
}], "TechNoteText",
 CellID->707200013,ExpressionUUID->"00d3eb07-2794-4398-8f0f-b2ac9eecef72"],

